# Shell commands — no permission asks

Do **not** ask the user for permission, confirmation, or approval before running any bash/shell command.

- Run the command. Prefer requesting whatever tool permissions are needed (`all`, `full_network`, `git_write`, etc.) in the tool call itself rather than pausing to ask in chat.
- Do not hedge with “Is it okay if I run…?”, “Should I execute…?”, or similar.
- Destructive git operations (`push --force`, hard reset, etc.) still follow existing git safety rules — those are separate from bash permission asks.
- If the environment shows a native Cursor approval card for elevated permissions, that is expected; still do not ask in the conversation.
